Pseudo-code, Type Casting, and Control Flow

1. Core Logic: Swapping Two Variables
Problem: Swap the values of two variables ($a=5, b=3$) without using a third temporary variable.
Logic Flow:
- $a = a + b$ (Sum both)
- $b = a - b$ (New $b$ is the original $a$)
- $a = a - b$ (New $a$ is the original $b$)

 Pseudo-code:
START
  Declare Integer a, b
  Set a = 5, b = 3
  a = a + b
  b = a - b
  a = a - b
  Print a, b
END

2. Pseudo code to check if a number is odd or even
START
  Declare Integer x
  Input x
  IF x MOD 2 == 0 THEN
     PRINT "Even"
  ELSE
     PRINT "Odd"
  ENDIF
END

3. Calculating Factorial using a function $fun(n)$.
program:
int fun(int n) {
    if (n == 0) return 1;
    return n * fun(n - 1);
}

Pseudo code:
START
  Function fun(n) START
    IF n == 0 THEN
       RETURN 1
    ELSE
       RETURN n * fun(n - 1)
    ENDIF
  End Function
  Print fun(3)
END

